    "title": "88-year-old hiker missing from Moreau Lake State Park - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Natalie St. Denis ,\n2 hours ago\nGANSEVOORT, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — New York State authorities are searching for an overdue hiker in Moreau Lake State Park. 88-year-old Albert Sakowicz started his hike at the Western Ridge Trailhead at about 9:30 a.m. on Wednesday, but has not returned.\nHe is described as a white man, standing 6 feet 2 inches tall, with blue eyes and grey hair. Officials say he also walks with a limp.\n88-year-old Albert Sakowicz (New York State Police) Get the latest news, weather, sports and entertainment delivered right to your inbox! Sakowicz is said to be an avid hiker, but his caretaker became concerned when he did not return by 1 p.m. on Wednesday, and contacted the state police.\nA search of the immediate area and the surrounding areas has been conducted, but he has not been located. The search was done in partnership with State Police Aviation, New York State Park Police and the New York State Department of Environmental Conservation Forest Rangers.\nDownload our WTEN+ streaming app on Roku, Fire TV and Apple TV! Anyone who has seen Sakowicz since Wednesday morning is asked to contact New York State Police at 518-457-6811. Authorities said a heavy police presence related to the search within the park should be anticipated.\nRead the latest from NEWS10:\nNEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader!\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
